    "text": "This is a greedy heuristic, not a provably optimal solver. The program repeatedly takes the vehicle that becomes free earliest and assigns it the unassigned ride with the best points-per-step ratio: (distance + bonus if it starts on time) divided by the number of steps from the vehicle's current time to that ride's finish. It skips rides the vehicle cannot complete by their latest finish. Each assignment takes O(N) to scan, and there are at most N assignments, so the worst case is about 10^8 simple operations. I have not compiled or run it against any data set.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long R, C, F, N, B, T;\n    cin >> R >> C >> F >> N >> B >> T;\n\n    vector<long long> A(N), Bc(N), X(N), Y(N), S(N), Fi(N);\n    for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) {\n        cin >> A[i] >> Bc[i] >> X[i] >> Y[i] >> S[i] >> Fi[i];\n    }\n\n    vector<long long> dist(N);\n    for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) {\n        dist[i] = llabs(X[i] - A[i]) + llabs(Y[i] - Bc[i]);\n    }\n\n    vector<bool> used(N, false);\n    vector<vector<int>> assigned(F);\n\n    // Vehicle state: (free time, vehicle id); position stored separately.\n    vector<long long> px(F, 0), py(F, 0), pt(F, 0);\n    priority_queue<pair<long long, int>, vector<pair<long long, int>>,\n                   greater<pair<long long, int>>> pq;\n    for (int v = 0; v < F; ++v) pq.push({0LL, v});\n\n    while (!pq.empty()) {\n        auto [t, v] = pq.top();\n        pq.pop();\n\n        int best = -1;\n        double bestVal = -1.0;\n        long long bestFinish = 0;\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) {\n            if (used[i]) continue;\n            long long toStart = llabs(px[v] - A[i]) + llabs(py[v] - Bc[i]);\n            long long start = max(t + toStart, S[i]);\n            long long finish = start + dist[i];\n            if (finish > Fi[i]) continue;\n            if (finish > T) continue;\n            double pts = (double)dist[i] + (start == S[i] ? (double)B : 0.0);\n            double val = pts / (double)(finish - t);\n            if (val > bestVal) {\n                bestVal = val;\n                best = i;\n                bestFinish = finish;\n            }\n        }\n\n        if (best < 0) continue; // this vehicle has no further feasible ride\n\n        used[best] = true;\n        assigned[v].push_back(best);\n        px[v] = X[best];\n        py[v] = Y[best];\n        pt[v] = bestFinish;\n        pq.push({bestFinish, v});\n    }\n\n    string out;\n    for (int v = 0; v < F; ++v) {\n        out += to_string(assigned[v].size());\n        for (int r : assigned[v]) {\n            out += ' ';\n            out += to_string(r);\n        }\n        out += '\\n';\n    }\n    cout << out;\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
